checks/audits/fed-rate--2026-09-16-unanimous-quarter-point-hike-2026-09-19-entailment.log:478:        <p data-layer="narrative">Seven weeks earlier, the committee had held the range at 3.50–3.75 percent by a {decision.julyVote.forHold}–{decision.julyVote.forIncrease} vote. The July minutes say most participants wanted more information before acting, while several already favored a quarter-point increase.<Cite s="fomc-statement-2026-07-29" passage="approved the following statement for release by a 9 – 3 vote" /><Cite s="fomc-minutes-2026-07-29" passage="most participants supported maintaining the current target range" /><Cite s="fomc-minutes-2026-07-29" passage="Several participants favored an increase of 25 basis points" /></p>
